{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's request is to implement `cmd/sum` for the go-unix-utils project as task #5505 in a code generation pipeline (cobbler-scaffold stitch phase). Specifically, the task requires implementing srd078-sum requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, and R1.4, which cover the default BSD checksum computation. Two files must be created: `cmd/sum/main.go` and `cmd/sum/sum_test.go`. The implementation must pass differential testing against the GNU reference binary `gsum` from Homebrew coreutils.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - BSD checksum algorithm: 16-bit rotating checksum where for each byte, the checksum is right-rotated by 1 bit, then the byte value is added. Block size is 1024 bytes.\n   - Output format: `CHECKSUM BLOCKS FILENAME` (with filename for file args) or `CHECKSUM BLOCKS` (for stdin, filename omitted)\n   - Block count: `ceil(total_bytes / 1024)` for BSD algorithm\n   - Differential testing pattern: build Go binary with `testutils.BuildBinary`, find reference binary with `exec.LookPath(\"gsum\")`, skip if not found, run `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - SIGPIPE handling: must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - Exit codes: 0 on success, 1 when any file cannot be opened\n   - Error handling: print error to stderr for unreadable files, continue processing remaining files\n   - LC_ALL=C must be set in test environments\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd078-sum.yaml` (READ)\n     - This is the SRD defining all requirements for the sum utility\n     - R1.1: BSD checksum computation, output \"CHECKSUM BLOCKS FILENAME\", block size 1024\n     - R1.2: Read from stdin when no files given, omit filename in output\n     - R1.3: Process multiple files in argument order, one line per file\n     - R1.4: Exit 1 on file open failure, print error to stderr, continue remaining files\n     - R2.1: -r flag selects BSD (default)\n     - R2.2: -s flag selects System V algorithm (16-bit sum, block size 512)\n     - R3.3: SIGPIPE handling via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n     - Non-goals: no modern hash algorithms\n   \n   - `cmd/sum/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Sum utility implementing R1.1-R1.4\n   \n   - `cmd/sum/sum_test.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests against gsum reference binary\n\n   - Key existing source patterns to follow (from project_context):\n     - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`: `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` function\n     - `pkg/testutils/build.go`: `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` pattern\n     - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go`: `DiffTest` struct and `RunDiffTests` function\n     - `pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go`: Pattern for processing multiple files with stdin fallback (similar structure needed)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only one file was read before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the BSD checksum algorithm and output format requirements\n   - Identified that the task scope is R1.1-R1.4 only (default BSD checksum), but R2 (-r/-s flags) and R3.3 (SIGPIPE) should also be considered given design decisions D1\n   - The task does NOT include R2.1, R2.2, R3.1, R3.2 in scope, only R1.1-R1.4\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely detailed task prompt providing all project context, SRDs, source code, execution constitution, go style constitution, and specific task instructions for implementing cmd/sum with requirements R1.1-R1.4 from srd078-sum\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Request to create a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/sum/main.go` implementing BSD checksum computation (R1.1-R1.4)\n   - Create `cmd/sum/sum_test.go` with differential tests against gsum\n   - Run `go build -o bin/sum ./cmd/sum/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/sum/` to check for issues (AC2)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/sum/ -count=1` to verify tests pass (AC3)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just read the SRD file `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd078-sum.yaml` to understand the requirements for the sum utility. I was about to plan and implement the two source files (`cmd/sum/main.go` and `cmd/sum/sum_test.go`) when the summarization request came.\n\n   The SRD revealed:\n   - BSD checksum: 16-bit rotating checksum, block size 1024\n   - Output: \"CHECKSUM BLOCKS FILENAME\" or \"CHECKSUM BLOCKS\" (stdin)\n   - Must handle multiple files, error on unreadable files (exit 1), continue processing\n   - Task scope is specifically R1.1-R1.4 only, plus SIGPIPE per design decision D1\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write both `cmd/sum/main.go` and `cmd/sum/sum_test.go` in a single pass following the implementation strategy from go_style_constitution. The main.go needs: SIGPIPE handler, BSD checksum algorithm (right-rotate + add for each byte), block count calculation (ceil(bytes/1024)), output formatting, stdin fallback, multi-file processing with error handling. The test file needs differential tests using `testutils.BuildBinary` and `exec.LookPath(\"gsum\")` with cases covering: single file, stdin, multiple files, and nonexistent file error handling.\n\n   This directly corresponds to the task description: \"deliverable_type: code\" with files `cmd/sum/main.go` (create) and `cmd/sum/sum_test.go` (create), implementing srd078-sum R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5505/66bddae1-6d45-4a77-8667-ab4009bb834e.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off wit